From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: brennoflavio <contato@brennoflavio.com.br>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 14:39:41 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] webapi: handle optional HTMLAllCollection lookups like Chrome

The Sephora SDK invokes document.all() with zero arguments. The old bridge
required an argument and threw TypeError; Chrome returns null. Accept the
optional legacy lookup argument, preserve explicit null DOMString conversion,
recognize canonical array-index strings, and return null for callable misses.
Share this lookup algorithm with item(), including its optional-argument arity,
while leaving absent indexed/named properties undefined and Symbols rejected.

Update three existing callable-miss expectations rather than adding tests.
Temporary isolated local Chrome/native reductions verify omitted/undefined/null,
index/name/object/Symbol coercion, selected element identity, and item arity.
All 1658 upstream tests pass. Scoped VM/native-binding captures confirm the SDK
call changes from InvalidArgument/TypeError to a null return. No binary POST
is recorded in that diagnostic follow-up; this is not a complete submission fix.

Temporary Promise/VM/binding hooks were removed from the development worktree.
---
 .../tests/document/all_collection.html        |  6 +--
 .../webapi/collections/HTMLAllCollection.zig  | 41 +++++++++++--------
 2 files changed, 26 insertions(+), 21 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/browser/tests/document/all_collection.html b/src/browser/tests/document/all_collection.html
index 9711e5a..eed2e7e 100644
--- a/src/browser/tests/document/all_collection.html
+++ b/src/browser/tests/document/all_collection.html
@@ -51,10 +51,10 @@
     testing.expectEqual('DIV', document.all(4).tagName);
     testing.expectEqual('DIV', document.all('first').tagName);
     testing.expectEqual('First', document.all('first').textContent);
-    testing.expectEqual(undefined, document.all('second'));
+    testing.expectEqual(null, document.all('second'));
     testing.expectEqual('P', document.all('third').tagName);
-    testing.expectEqual(undefined, document.all(999));
-    testing.expectEqual(undefined, document.all('nonexistent'));
+    testing.expectEqual(null, document.all(999));
+    testing.expectEqual(null, document.all('nonexistent'));
 
     let count = 0;
     for (const el of document.all) {
diff --git a/src/browser/webapi/collections/HTMLAllCollection.zig b/src/browser/webapi/collections/HTMLAllCollection.zig
index 03e0cb7..13d11a0 100644
--- a/src/browser/webapi/collections/HTMLAllCollection.zig
+++ b/src/browser/webapi/collections/HTMLAllCollection.zig
@@ -1,6 +1,8 @@
